{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786429317,"nonce":"yl3ueaft5FtJaQSjvGJimguM1ec=","title":"The Slack app manifest ships an Acknowledge button that can never work","message":"**What is wrong.** `deploy/slack/manifest.yaml` sets `socket_mode_enabled: true` and declares no `request_url`, while `docs/setup/slack.md` states that Socket Mode is not implemented and that the Request URL is mandatory for interactivity.\n\nAn operator who follows the setup doc and installs from the manifest gets an app whose Acknowledge button cannot reach oto — the interaction has nowhere to POST. The endpoint itself is fine (`POST /api/v1/integrations/slack/interactions` verifies the HMAC and enqueues the ack); the app is simply not configured to call it.\n\n**Why it matters.** Ack is the single act oto asks of a human (ADR 0013), and the button is on every card oto posts. This is the same user-visible symptom as the bug filed in 85da108 — press it and nothing happens — arriving through configuration instead of code, and it lands on every fresh install that follows the documented path.\n\n**Where.** `deploy/slack/manifest.yaml:~130`, `docs/setup/slack.md` §1.\n\n**Done when.** The manifest declares the interactivity `request_url` pointing at `/api/v1/integrations/slack/interactions` (with the placeholder host the rest of the doc uses), `socket_mode_enabled` reflects what oto actually implements, and installing from the manifest by following `docs/setup/slack.md` produces a working Acknowledge button. `docs/setup/slack.md` §1 currently carries the correction inline as a stopgap.","files":null}]}